      "caption": "\\frac12\\sin x\\le \\frac12x\\le \\frac12\\tan x",
      "seconds": 11.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "For a positive angle less than pi over two, the inner triangle lies inside the sector, and the sector lies inside the tangent triangle. Their areas therefore increase from left to right.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "title": "Remove the common factor",
      "component": "comparison",
      "parameters": {
        "left_title": "Before",
        "right_title": "After",
        "row_labels": [
          "multiply by 2"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "\\frac12\\sin x\\le\\frac12x\\le\\frac12\\tan x",
            "\\sin x\\le x\\le\\tan x"
          ]
        ],
        "highlight": [
          0
        ]
      },
      "caption": "\\sin x\\le x\\le\\tan x",
      "seconds": 6.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Multiply every part by two. Because two is positive, the order does not change.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "title": "Rewrite tangent",
      "component": "flow_diagram",
      "parameters": {
        "stages": [
          "\\sin x\\le x\\le\\tan x",
          "\\tan x=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}",
          "x>0,\\ \\cos x>0"
        ],
        "highlight": [
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      "caption": "\\sin x\\le x\\le\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}",
      "seconds": 10.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Use tan x equals sin x over cos x. In our domain, x and cos x are both positive, so the next divisions will be safe.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "title": "The upper bound",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\sin x\\le x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\le 1",
      "seconds": 8.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "From sin x less than or equal to x, divide by the positive number x. This places sin x over x below one.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "title": "The lower bound",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "x\\le\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x\\cos x\\le\\sin x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\cos x\\le\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
      "seconds": 12.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Start with x less than or equal to sin x over cos x. Multiply by positive cos x, then divide by positive x. The result places cos x below sin x over x.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "title": "Positive-side squeeze",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\cos x\\le\\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\le 1\\qquad\\left(0<x<\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)",
      "seconds": 5.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Combining the two results gives the complete squeeze for positive x near zero.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "title": "Symmetry across zero",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\frac{\\sin(-x)}{-x}=\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
      "seconds": 12.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Because sine is odd, changing x to negative x changes both the numerator and denominator's signs. The signs cancel, so the ratio is even and the same bounds apply on the negative side.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "title": "Both bounds converge",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "cos(x)",
        "x_min": -1.5,
        "x_max": 1.5,
        "label": "\\cos x",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\lim_{x\\to0}\\cos x=\\cos 0=1,\\qquad \\lim_{x\\to0}1=1",
      "seconds": 11.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "As x approaches zero, cosine approaches cos zero, which is one. The constant upper bound is already one. Both sides therefore meet at the same limiting value.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "title": "Apply the squeeze theorem",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\cos x\\le\\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\le 1\\quad\\mbox{and}\\quad \\lim_{x\\to0}\\cos x=\\lim_{x\\to0}1=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x}=1",
      "seconds": 9.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "A function trapped between two functions with the same limit must share that limit. Therefore sin x over x approaches one from both sides of zero.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "title": "FINAL ANSWER",
      "component": "function_plot",
      "parameters": {
        "expr": "sin(x)/x",
        "x_min": -3.0,
        "x_max": 3.0,
        "label": "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}",
        "y_min": 0.0,
        "y_max": 1.2,
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\boxed{\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x}=1}",
      "seconds": 11.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "",
      "narration": "Thus, when x is measured in radians, the ratio of sin x to x approaches one as x approaches zero from either side. Near zero, sin x is approximately x.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    }
  ]
